<title>ESTONIA: LONG-TERM INTERBANK LOAN RATES FALL.</title>
<headline>LONG-TERM INTERBANK LOAN RATES FALL.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overnight interbank rates on</p>
<p>longer periods decreased over the last week while the rates on</p>
<p>one-week money were stable, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The attention that was on the shorter terms has gone to the</p>
<p>longer periods,&quot; said Ege Metsandi from Hansapank interest rate</p>
<p>product department.</p>
<p>&quot;The rates should go up from the second week of May, when</p>
<p>large loan repayment deadlines are due,&quot; Metsandi added.</p>
<p>&quot;It is going to take some money out of the local market,&quot;</p>
<p>she added.</p>
<p>Next week the rates should remain stable, with slight</p>
<p>changes, she added.</p>
<p> TALIBOR/TALIBID   One Week   One Month   Three months</p>
<p> April 16	   4.50/3.50   5.92/4.92     7.43/6.43</p>
<p> April 09	   4.50/3.50   6.08/5.08     7.52/6.52</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 630 8400,</p>
<p>reuters@reuters.ee</p>
